AB  - Local disease in NSCLC refers to early stage lung cancer (stage I or stage II). Local disease has a more favorable prognosis than later stage disease, largely due to the ability to consider treatment with curative intent in this group of patients. Treatment options include surgery, radiotherapy and systemic therapy, either alone or in combination. Management options in local disease are guided by patient fitness and patient preference alongside disease-specific features including location and histology. This article discusses in detail the management of local disease and explores the associated risk assessment and appropriate patient selection for each treatment modality. © 2022 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved
