UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-39149105650&partnerID=40&md5=4165f2e0994ca77eced652e500be4954
AD  - Klinik für Thoraxchirurgie, Bremen, Germany
AB  - The surgery treatment of carcinomas has to follow criteria adapted to the tumor stage. Only the early stage diseases (IA/IB) are potentially surgically curable. In advanced stages (II-III) thoracic surgery is integrated in multimodality treatment approaches (neadjuvant chemotherapy, adjuvant chemotherapy, adjuvant radiotherapy). The »gold standard« operation is anatomic lobectomy or pneumonectomy with systematic mediastinal lymph node dissection. Sleeve resections of the bronchial tree or the pulmonal artery are established procedures. Limited resection (segmentectomy/wegde resection) and the decision for extended resection of the pericard, left atrium, thoracic aorta, spine or esophagus should be the exception because of missing evidence for the patients benefit in the literature. In rare conditions surgical treatment for palliation could be necessary without curative intention. Operative treatment concepts for bronchial carcinoma should always be appointed in an interdisciplinary approach.
