AB  - Further refinement of surgery for early stage NSCLC will come from a variety of proposed and ongoing clinical trials. The Surgical Oncology Group of the American College of Surgeons is planning studies on the role of possitron-emission tomography scanning in preoperative staging, whether lymph node dissection improves cure rates over lymph node sampling alone, and the role of genetic markers, immunohistochemical staining, bone marrow examination, and pleural lavage as prognostic indicators. Ongoing Intergroup trials seek to determine the role of 13-cis-retinoic acid as a chemoprevention agent for second primaries and the role of thoracoscopic wedge resection followed by radiation therapy for patients with severely compromised pulmonary function.
